From 989077011b498251149783bd1523983cd0914b1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:33:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] palmLegacyManager: route calls via PulseAudio card profiles
 and ports

Fills in applyCallRouting(). module-palm-policy moves streams between virtual
sinks, which is not enough for a carrier call: the ALSA card has to be moved
onto its voicecall profile, and the handset sink and source onto the right
physical ports. Only libpulse can do either, so this opens its own pa_context
-- PulseAudioLink keeps its own private, and audio-service has been driving
LuneOS calls exactly this way for years.

The walk is card profile first (a profile switch replaces the card's sinks and
sources, so port selection has to follow it, not race it), then the sink port
(earpiece / speaker / wired headset by scenario), then the source port
(built-in or headset mic), with the capture mute re-asserted so an unmuted
call cannot be defeated by a stale port-level mute. Sinks without an
output-earpiece port and sources that are sink monitors are skipped, so HDMI,
USB and loopback devices are left alone.

Dual-SIM devices get voicecall-voicemmode1 preferred over plain voicecall,
matching the Palm-era behaviour. Leaving a call restores the
highest-priority available profile.

PA_CONTEXT_NOFAIL means audiod starting before PulseAudio is not fatal;
the state callback re-applies a live call once the connection is up, and
clears the applied mode on disconnect so the next transition is re-pushed
rather than swallowed by updateCallMode()'s early return.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific legacy API]
